      "content": "I can't even imagine how isolating and disorienting that must feel after losing a valued part of your life. It sounds like recovering your sense of purpose and feeling like you can make meaningful contributions once more will take time. Acknowledge your feelings of drifting and despair—they are valid reactions to such a profound loss. However, rebuilding your life and discovering new sources of fulfillment is possible. It might involve exploring different interests and activities outside your current research work. This doesn't mean leaving your field behind; it's about finding joy and connection in other aspects of life while also honoring the passion that led you here in the first place. During this time, it may also help to reflect on the vast range of ways one can impact and contribute to the world, even beyond academic research. Please don't hesitate to seek a supportive community or professional guidance. There is hope and a path forward, even when it's not immediately clear.",
      "source": "target",
